        "title": "fix: require full frontmatter delimiter lines",
        "body": "Closes #101769\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where Markdown beginning with dash-prefixed text such as `---not` or `----` could be mistaken for YAML frontmatter, causing metadata or body content to be parsed, stripped, or dropped.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nFrontmatter now starts and ends only on complete `---` delimiter lines after BOM and newline normalization. The shared extractor owns that contract, and agent prompt/session loading, workspace and dev templates, Claude bundle commands, hooks, skills, and workshop proposals all use the same implementation instead of copied prefix checks.\n\n## User Impact\n\nOrdinary dash-prefixed Markdown remains intact. Valid frontmatter, including delimiter lines with trailing whitespace, continues to parse normally.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Exact reviewed head: `6da57533d31aab11424e2522f6edeb0efe9b9efb`.\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs packages/markdown-core/src/frontmatter.test.ts src/plugins/bundle-commands.test.ts src/skills/workshop/frontmatter.test.ts src/skills/loading/session.test.ts src/agents/sessions/prompt-templates.test.ts src/hooks/frontmatter.test.ts src/skills/loading/frontmatter.test.ts` passed: 7 files, 50 tests.\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/agents/workspace.test.ts src/agents/workspace-templates.test.ts` passed: 2 files, 60 tests.\n- Testbox-through-Crabbox `tbx_01kwywqb0qad3bjj0kh9wg5be8`: `pnpm check:changed` passed with no temp-directory warnings; typechecks, core lint, import cycles, and guards were clean. Actions run `28888585400`.\n- Fresh Codex autoreview on the final branch diff: clean, no accepted/actionable findings.\n- `git diff --check` passed.\n",
